{
  "id": 21,
  "name": "adaptive_regret_with_cluster_modulated_spread",
  "intent": "Building on the regret-aware parent, this variant adapts the regret coefficient by remaining-tour fraction (0.30-0.50), amplifying future-flexibility concern early when selection mistakes propagate farthest. The progress gain on the return penalty is softened slightly (0.25 vs 0.30) to avoid over-closing the loop late. The spread penalty is dampened by cluster density: in clustered regimes where high spread reflects natural variance, it is halved; in uniform regimes, it stays at full strength. Hypothesis: early-game regret amplification targets the uniform-instance weakness without disturbing clustered or grid performance.",
  "tags": [
    "regret",
    "cluster"
  ],
  "code": "def priority(f):\n    progress = f['progress']\n    distance = f['distance']\n    return_distance = f['return_distance']\n    nearest_remaining = f['nearest_remaining']\n    regret = f['regret']\n    spread = f['spread']\n    cluster_density = f['cluster_density']\n    return_weight = 0.20 + 0.25 * progress\n    regret_weight = 0.30 + 0.20 * (1.0 - progress)\n    return_penalty = return_weight * return_distance\n    regret_term = regret_weight * regret\n    spread_penalty = 0.05 * spread * (1.0 - 0.5 * cluster_density)\n    return -distance + return_penalty + regret_term - 0.10 * nearest_remaining - spread_penalty",
  "source": "live_llm",
